WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
A fixed-time guarantee assumes one fixed look.
This theorem controls every sample size from four onward on one event.

00:08.000 --> 00:20.000
The process Lean checks: adapted, measurable, integrable increments;
boundedness, conditional centering, and a conditional moment bound almost everywhere.

00:20.000 --> 00:33.000
Every sample size n >= 4 belongs to one checked factor-four epoch.

00:33.000 --> 00:46.000
Polynomial confidence weights telescope exactly to one.

00:46.000 --> 01:00.000
One fixed tilt per epoch, chosen before observing the path.

01:00.000 --> 01:14.000
Countable subadditivity yields one two-sided event.
The width is evaluated at each plotted integer; the path is illustrative.

01:14.000 --> 01:26.000
A checked log-log confidence sequence: every sample size n >= 4,
with complement real mass at most delta.
